    "title": "Sudoers policy modified",
    "desc": "A program edited the sudo policy - /etc/sudoers or a drop-in under /etc/sudoers.d/ - via a file tool (tee, sed, cp, mv, dd, install) or any process whose file access touched those paths. Granting an account NOPASSWD, disabling tty_tickets, or setting an unlimited timestamp_timeout rewrites who can become root and how freely (MITRE T1548.003): it is a durable privilege-escalation and persistence foothold. privilege_escalation_attempt catches running sudo; this catches rewriting the rules sudo enforces. visudo editing by hand is interactive and not matched here.",
